{
  "id": "ss.char.egg",
  "name": "Egg",
  "description": "A survivor that has not finished hatching — the youngest of the eight and the one the fiction is least kind to, because its feelers were never given a signal to lose. Hatchling proportions: a head too big for the body, short limbs, and a soft pale torso still showing the grub's segment lines under the plate that never grew. The helmet is the egg it came out of, with the crack it came out through still running down it and two tufts of shell-hair standing off the top. Its weapon is what a thing this young can use: a pair of Soldier mandibles bound at the elbow, carried crossed on its back and thrown so they come back. Same dead organ as the rest, same place, and the feelers are stubs — it never grew those either. Bare chitin cold slate; the plate is unlit shell-white. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
